"Status" = "狀態";
"Steady frame rate" = "穩定畫面更新率";
"Steady frame rate puts rendering ahead of everything else MuffinEMU does: the graphics thread gets first call on the fastest cores, each frame is shown at the game's own Wii U frame rate (steady, and never faster than the console), and debugging extras are skipped. Every shader the game has used before is built while the game loads, so those never cause a hitch or a flicker. The first time something brand new appears, its shader has to be built: \"Wait for it\" holds the frame until it's ready (a short hitch, never a missing object), \"Keep going\" draws without it once (no hitch, but it can be missing for a moment). Either way it's saved, so it happens only once. This choice wins over the Accuracy and Speed performance profiles and Compile shaders in the background. Takes effect the next time you start a game." = "「穩定畫面更新率」讓轉譯優先於 MuffinEMU 所做的其他一切：圖形執行緒優先使用最快的核心，每個影格都以遊戲本身的 Wii U 畫面更新率顯示（穩定，且絕不比主機更快），並略過除錯附加功能。遊戲曾經使用過的每個著色器都會在遊戲載入時建置，因此它們絕不會造成卡頓或閃爍。全新的內容第一次出現時，必須建置其著色器：「等一下」會暫停該影格直到準備好（短暫卡頓，但絕不缺少物件），「繼續進行」則不使用它先繪製一次（不卡頓，但可能短暫缺少）。無論哪種都會儲存，所以只會發生一次。此選擇的優先順序高於「準確度」和「速度」效能設定檔，以及「在背景編譯著色器」。於下次啟動遊戲時生效。";
